From 25a2416a6a7f128f640aa6ff47b30329d2acb002 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kris Williams <115474+kriswill@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 15:22:27 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] devenv-shell: hold virtual replies behind outstanding
 physical queries

The shell session answers CSI 6n (CPR), CSI 5n and the mode 2048 DECRQM
from the virtual terminal while forwarding OSC colour queries, DA, XTVERSION
and the other allowlisted queries to the physical terminal. A program that
sends `OSC 11 ; ?` followed by `CSI 6 n` and reads until the cursor report
(termenv, hence gh, glow and every lipgloss v1 user) therefore received the
CPR first, stopped reading, and left the colour reply in its tty input for
the shell to consume as keystrokes.

Count forwarded queries that expect an answer, hold captured virtual replies
while any is outstanding, and release them once the physical replies have
been written to the child. A 250 ms timeout covers terminals that never
answer, so a CPR is delayed rather than lost.

Verified against Ghostty inside `devenv shell`: the query pair now comes
back in order and gh/glow leave nothing in the tty buffer.

Ref: cachix/devenv#3130
